Python & Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)

Overview

This repository contains Python programming concepts from beginner to intermediate level, with a strong focus on Object-Oriented Programming (OOP). It includes theory, hands-on examples, and practice exercises to build a solid programming foundation.

Topics Covered

- Python Basics
- Variables & Data Types
- Operators
- Conditional Statements
- Loops
- Functions
- Modules & Packages
- File Handling
- Exception Handling
- Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
  - Classes & Objects
  - Constructors
  - Encapsulation
  - Inheritance
  - Polymorphism
  - Abstraction
  - Method Overriding
  - Method Overloading (Concept)
- Iterators & Generators
- Lambda Functions
- List, Dictionary & Set Comprehensions

Folder Structure

Python-and-OOPs/
│── Notes/
│── Practice/
│── Assignments/
│── Mini Projects/
└── README.md

Learning Outcomes

- Build a strong understanding of Python fundamentals.
- Apply OOP principles to write clean and reusable code.
- Improve problem-solving and logical thinking.
- Prepare for coding interviews and technical assessments.

Tools Used

- Python 3.x
- Jupyter Notebook
- VS Code

Status

Completed basic concepts and continuously adding practice problems and mini projects.
